<title>RUSSIA: Russia gives Norsi-oil chief ministry post-agency.</title>
<headline>Russia gives Norsi-oil chief ministry post-agency.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian government has named Sergei Kirienko, president of an oil company based in the region where reformer Boris Nemtsov was governor, as first deputy fuel and energy minister, Interfax news agency reported on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The Fuel and Energy Ministry could not immediately confirm that Kirienko, president of Nizhny Novogorod-based Norsi-oil company, had been named to the post.</p>
<p>First Deputy Prime Minister Boris Nemtsov is also Fuel and Energy Minister. Before being named First Deputy Prime Minister, Nemtsov was governor of the Nizhny Novgorod region.</p>
<p>--Moscow newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
